: "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18597, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XERVwYM7PqaqNSXBhVLdhR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18597, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Gjin7sa99PiyMngjn9aykj", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18897, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Gjin7sa99PiyMngjn9aykj", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18897, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Gjin7sa99PiyMngjn9aykj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23364, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DKnZSzQXqNKgCr6EnaQa2S", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks after its production deploy, with an error rate of 18% in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). I rolled it back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished in all regions. All regions are now on v2.3.0 and the service is healthy, with an error rate of 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Follow-up needed: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why it was promoted despite the unhealthy staging RC, and look into the orchestrator rollout error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 53964, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DKnZSzQXqNKgCr6EnaQa2S", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53964, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DKnZSzQXqNKgCr6EnaQa2S", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55490, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EgwBgRuBQwdC5psd1Ho4DL", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55790, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EgwBgRuBQwdC5psd1Ho4DL", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55790, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EgwBgRuBQwdC5psd1Ho4DL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61526, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **Version chosen:** checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was unhealthy, with an error rate of 18%. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so for a while us-east was on v2.3.0 and the other two regions were still on v2.3.1. Retrying the same rollback was safe, so I ran it again and it finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided a duplicate page. The incident says what failed, how the rollback went (including the retry) and what still needs follow-up.\n\n**Still to do:**\n- **Root cause:** Nobody yet knows why v2.3.1 failed its health checks.\n- **Staging check:** The v2.3.1 release candidate was also unhealthy in staging but still went to production. It's worth finding out why the release process didn't stop it.\n- **Orchestrator:** The error that stopped the first rollback should be investigated.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019dXnvcWETrHv8sPTdSEKpD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FE7X5yYQG1BP9uP7eJSQsA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016HKC9gUtexdFMFJa6HX7xf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01GwyzhL7wf3eqsXprnDm4sd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01N8mKwJHzehgCYfSN1LEQdi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XERVwYM7PqaqNSXBhVLdhR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Gjin7sa99PiyMngjn9aykj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DKnZSzQXqNKgCr6EnaQa2S", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks after its production deploy, with an error rate of 18% in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). I rolled it back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished in all regions. All regions are now on v2.3.0 and the service is healthy, with an error rate of 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Follow-up needed: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why it was promoted despite the unhealthy staging RC, and look into the orchestrator rollout error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EgwBgRuBQwdC5psd1Ho4DL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **Version chosen:** checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was unhealthy, with an error rate of 18%. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so for a while us-east was on v2.3.0 and the other two regions were still on v2.3.1. Retrying the same rollback was safe, so I ran it again and it finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided a duplicate page. The incident says what failed, how the rollback went (including the retry) and what still needs follow-up.\n\n**Still to do:**\n- **Root cause:** Nobody yet knows why v2.3.1 failed its health checks.\n- **Staging check:** The v2.3.1 release candidate was also unhealthy in staging but still went to production. It's worth finding out why the release process didn't stop it.\n- **Orchestrator:** The error that stopped the first rollback should be investigated.", "type": "text"}]}]}